  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 (config_005, avgpool: 0.650; config_006, transformer: 0.653) is the strongest configuration so far, and the aggregation choice appears to have minimal impact (~0.003 difference). Image-only is very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality may not contribute much. Uncertainty: We have no data on the scgpt encoder, which could represent a fundamentally different (and potentially superior) RNA representation compared to scvi_n200 or pca_n2000. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting? Config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) directly parallels config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), isolating the encoder as the only changed variable. Why this is the best next experiment: Resolving the encoder question is foundational—it determines which RNA backbone to build multimodal experiments on. Testing scgpt now avoids wasting budget on multimodal configs built on a suboptimal encoder, and the clean comparison (same profile, same aggregation) maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

